Subject: [#94-10-460] BABY: REproduction

While I'd like to see people being able to genetically modify their
own bodies, I think that the methods will be developed quite a bit
later than "designer babies".

Choosing genes for a new person is tricky, but at least you don't have 
to figure out how to make changes whose intermediate stages won't
damage a living person.

Also, it's possible to observe how developement goes from egg and
sperm to human being--there's no natural model (that I know of)
to work from for genetic modification.

I'm not saying that genetic modification of living beings is impossible--
just that it will be very challenging to work out.

